Package: llmsa
Type: Package
Title: Measurement System Analysis for Pipelines Built on Large Language Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Daniel Andreas", "Moj", , "daniel.moj2@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0008-1594-6065"))
Description: Treats a pipeline built on a large language model (LLM) as a
    measurement system and validates it with the tools that analytical
    laboratories already use: crossed precision studies with variance
    components (gauge repeatability and reproducibility), attribute
    agreement with kappa statistics and Krippendorff's alpha, bias against
    a reference, Plackett-Burman screening of robustness against prompt and
    formatting perturbations, simulation-based planning of study size,
    Westgard-rule control charts for ongoing system suitability, and a
    reproducible validation report. The methods follow Burdick, Borror and
    Montgomery (2003) <doi:10.1080/00224065.2003.11980232>, Plackett and
    Burman (1946) <doi:10.1093/biomet/33.4.305>, Lenth (1989)
    <doi:10.1080/00401706.1989.10488595> and Westgard et al. (1981)
    <doi:10.1093/clinchem/27.3.493>. The package is pipeline-agnostic: any
    backend that turns a prompt and a model identifier into a text
    response can be validated, and results produced elsewhere can be
    imported.
